# The courier ref this repository's gate reads. One line: a 40-character commit
# sha. NEVER a branch — a floating ref would make identity's gate depend on
# courier's unreleased work, so a type courier added yesterday reds a tree that
# changed nothing.
# The gate job checks this ref out to `../courier`, outside the tree, where
# `TestCouriersTypesAgreeWithCouriersDocument` (internal/courier/recorded_test.go)
# parses the `NotificationType` enum out of its `openapi.yaml` and fails unless
# it equals this tree's `Type*` constants in both directions.
# Move it with the vocabulary diff in front of you: the pinned commit's enum must
# name exactly the six types in `identityTypes` (welcome, password_reset,
# team_invitation, account_security, email_change_current, email_change_new),
# and a bump that adds a type lands in the same commit as the `Type*` constant
# it requires.
